{"code":"51-3092.00","title":"Food Batchmakers","description":"Set up and operate equipment that mixes or blends ingredients used in the manufacturing of food products. Includes candy makers and cheese makers.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":6.09,"share":0.3952},"I":{"score":2.11,"share":0.0862},"A":{"score":1.91,"share":0.0707},"S":{"score":1.5,"share":0.0388},"E":{"score":2.62,"share":0.1258},"C":{"score":4.65,"share":0.2834}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":4919,"text":"Record production and test data for each food product batch, such as the ingredients used, temperature, test results, and time cycle.","core":true,"importance":4.77,"relevance":87.65,"frequency":6.06},{"id":4921,"text":"Clean and sterilize vats and factory processing areas.","core":true,"importance":4.73,"relevance":91.03,"frequency":5.26},{"id":4935,"text":"Test food product samples for moisture content, acidity level, specific gravity, or butter-fat content, and continue processing until desired levels are reached.","core":false,"importance":4.66,"relevance":58.15,"frequency":5.91},{"id":4924,"text":"Set up, operate, and tend equipment that cooks, mixes, blends, or processes ingredients in the manufacturing of food products, according to formulas or recipes.","core":true,"importance":4.65,"relevance":93.76,"frequency":6.03},{"id":4925,"text":"Mix or blend ingredients, according to recipes, using a paddle or an agitator, or by controlling vats that heat and mix ingredients.","core":true,"importance":4.61,"relevance":82.56,"frequency":6.05},{"id":4933,"text":"Inspect vats after cleaning to ensure that fermentable residue has been removed.","core":false,"importance":4.61,"relevance":61.22,"frequency":5.61},{"id":4926,"text":"Follow recipes to produce food products of specified flavor, texture, clarity, bouquet, or color.","core":true,"importance":4.56,"relevance":93.09,"frequency":6.08},{"id":4931,"text":"Give directions to other workers who are assisting in the batchmaking process.","core":true,"importance":4.56,"relevance":71.37,"frequency":6.1},{"id":4927,"text":"Select and measure or weigh ingredients, using English or metric measures and balance scales.","core":true,"importance":4.55,"relevance":68.45,"frequency":6.05},{"id":4922,"text":"Press switches and turn knobs to start, adjust, and regulate equipment, such as beaters, extruders, discharge pipes, and salt pumps.","core":true,"importance":4.53,"relevance":82.98,"frequency":5.96},{"id":4930,"text":"Fill processing or cooking containers, such as kettles, rotating cookers, pressure cookers, or vats, with ingredients, by opening valves, by starting pumps or injectors, or by hand.","core":false,"importance":4.53,"relevance":63.63,"frequency":6.17},{"id":4929,"text":"Determine mixing sequences, based on knowledge of temperature effects and of the solubility of specific ingredients.","core":true,"importance":4.51,"relevance":78.87,"frequency":5.74},{"id":4923,"text":"Observe and listen to equipment to detect possible malfunctions, such as leaks or plugging, and report malfunctions or undesirable tastes to supervisors.","core":true,"importance":4.5,"relevance":87.13,"frequency":5.99},{"id":4943,"text":"Manipulate products, by hand or using machines, to separate, spread, knead, spin, cast, cut, pull, or roll products.","core":false,"importance":4.49,"relevance":45.94,"frequency":6.32},{"id":4920,"text":"Observe gauges and thermometers to determine if the mixing chamber temperature is within specified limits, and turn valves to control the temperature.","core":true,"importance":4.47,"relevance":82.99,"frequency":6.12},{"id":4939,"text":"Cool food product batches on slabs or in water-cooled kettles.","core":false,"importance":4.46,"relevance":38.63,"frequency":5.89},{"id":4928,"text":"Turn valve controls to start equipment and to adjust operation to maintain product quality.","core":true,"importance":4.4,"relevance":71.87,"frequency":5.66},{"id":4941,"text":"Modify cooking and forming operations based on the results of sampling processes, adjusting time cycles and ingredients to achieve desired qualities, such as firmness or texture.","core":true,"importance":4.38,"relevance":68.56,"frequency":5.58},{"id":4942,"text":"Place products on carts or conveyors to transfer them to the next stage of processing.","core":false,"importance":4.35,"relevance":63.38,"frequency":6.02},{"id":4932,"text":"Homogenize or pasteurize material to prevent separation or to obtain prescribed butterfat content, using a homogenizing device.","core":false,"importance":4.33,"relevance":45.81,"frequency":5.93},{"id":4938,"text":"Grade food products according to government regulations or according to type, color, bouquet, and moisture content.","core":false,"importance":4.33,"relevance":64.63,"frequency":6.02},{"id":4940,"text":"Operate refining machines to reduce the particle size of cooked batches.","core":false,"importance":4.29,"relevance":40.24,"frequency":6.03},{"id":4934,"text":"Examine, feel, and taste product samples during production to evaluate quality, color, texture, flavor, and bouquet, and document the results.","core":true,"importance":4.28,"relevance":70.22,"frequency":5.91},{"id":4936,"text":"Formulate or modify recipes for specific kinds of food products.","core":false,"importance":4.28,"relevance":53.66,"frequency":4.46},{"id":4937,"text":"Inspect and pack the final product.","core":false,"importance":4.16,"relevance":56.7,"frequency":5.67}],"activities":[{"id":"4.A.1.a.2","importance":4.44},{"id":"4.A.3.a.3","importance":4.42},{"id":"4.A.3.b.6","importance":4.33},{"id":"4.A.4.a.2","importance":4.28},{"id":"4.A.1.b.2","importance":4.16},{"id":"4.A.1.b.1","importance":4.06},{"id":"4.A.2.b.1","importance":4.02},{"id":"4.A.3.a.2","importance":3.89},{"id":"4.A.1.a.1","importance":3.83},{"id":"4.A.2.a.3","importance":3.76},{"id":"4.A.1.b.3","importance":3.73},{"id":"4.A.2.a.1","importance":3.73},{"id":"4.A.3.a.1","importance":3.73},{"id":"4.A.2.a.2","importance":3.56},{"id":"4.